# SonoJS docs site — cursor pointer

Applies to **this docs website** (`app/`, `components/`).

For **installable** components (`registry/`, `packages/ui`), see `.cursor/rules/sonojs-registry-cursor.mdc` — those also require `cursor-pointer`.

## Rule

On the SonoJS docs site, every clickable control must show a pointer cursor:

- `<button>`, custom click handlers, icon toggles, nav links that act as controls, tabs, ghost menu triggers
- Use Tailwind `cursor-pointer`
- Disabled / non-interactive: `cursor-not-allowed` or keep `disabled:pointer-events-none` — never `cursor-pointer` when disabled

```tsx
// ✅ Site chrome
<button type="button" className="cursor-pointer …" />
<Link href="/docs" className="cursor-pointer …" />
```
